{"idolatry":{"id":"4bf3685c-0728-4321-a9c1-ae57b8988e87","word":"idolatry","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"worship of idols","tags":["feminine"],"word":"idolatria"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"excessive admiration","tags":["feminine"],"word":"idolatria"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"excessive admiration","tags":["feminine"],"word":"veneração"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"The parish stank of idolatry, abominable rites were practiced in secret, and in all the bounds there was no one had a more evil name for the black traffic than one Alison Sempill, who bode at the Skerburnfoot.","ref":"1902, John Buchan, The Outgoing of the Tide:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[20,28]],"id":"8a109e41-3fdc-4a06-82f9-1285e5e762d9"},{"text":"Now the great obstacle in tracing the identity of any of the basic forms of worship lies in the vast number of names which appear in the ancient idolatries and mythologies, creating the illusion of a miscellany of gods, whereas many of these different names refer to the same deity. Thus the sun has been personified and worshipped under as many different names as there are nations on the surface of the earth.","ref":"1941, George Ryley Scott, Phallic Worship: A History of Sex and Sex Rites in Relation to the Religions of All Races from Antiquity to the Present Day, London: T. Werner Laurie, page 20:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[145,155]],"id":"33035874-b00a-4259-b811-2929691c0ce1"}],"topics":["lifestyle","religion"],"categories":["English terms with quotations","Quotation templates to be cleaned","en:Religion"],"links":[["religion","religion"],["worship","worship"],["idol","idol"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"avodah zarah"}],"raw_glosses":["(religion) The worship of idols."],"glosses":["The worship of idols."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"d10662d0-3bba-4478-a929-2075286d5e0d"},{"links":[["excessive","excessive"],["admiration","admiration"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"adoration"},{"word":"reverence"},{"word":"worship"}],"raw_glosses":["(figurative) The excessive admiration of somebody or something."],"glosses":["The excessive admiration of somebody or something."],"tags":["countable","figuratively","uncountable"],"id":"4a8101be-133f-4a3c-8e50-ea97ea30c468"}],"related":[{"word":"idol"},{"word":"idolater"},{"word":"idolatrisation"},{"word":"idolatrise"},{"word":"idolatrization"},{"word":"idolatrize"},{"word":"idolatrizer"},{"word":"idolatrous"},{"word":"idolatrously"},{"word":"idolatrousness"},{"word":"-latry"}],"synonyms":[]},"I don't think so":{"id":"0183b91b-4af8-45ba-8cd3-b7c86b8a5ad7","word":"I don't think so","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"I think that what has been said is untrue","word":"eu acho que não"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"I think that what has been said is untrue","word":"acho que não"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"sarcastic","word":"de jeito nenhum"}],"pos":"phrase","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Bob: Is this the right place to catch the bus?\nSuzy: I don't think so.","bold_text_offsets":[[53,69]],"type":"example","id":"8c0d7386-1178-47ef-a78e-c4b47b6448e8"}],"glosses":["I think what has been said is untrue."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"id":"045c9ad7-35ae-441f-9f79-9b1bf9ad82ca"},{"examples":[{"text":"Go out with you? Huh, I don't think so, sweetheart!","bold_text_offsets":[[22,38]],"type":"example","id":"16a3aa79-6fb2-43e1-9bcd-57a6d29bc024"}],"categories":["English sarcastic terms","English terms with usage examples"],"links":[["sarcastic","sarcastic"]],"raw_glosses":["(sarcastic) No, absolutely not (used to refuse or decline something proposed)."],"glosses":["No, absolutely not (used to refuse or decline something proposed)."],"tags":["sarcastic"],"id":"d23c4fcb-b6f5-40f2-8c92-0d0cd31d482c"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[{"sense":"I think what has been said is untrue","word":"I think not"},{"sense":"strong way to say no","word":"absolutely not"},{"sense":"strong way to say no","word":"hardly"},{"sense":"strong way to say no","word":"not in a million years"},{"sense":"strong way to say no","word":"not on your life"},{"tags":["British"],"sense":"strong way to say no","word":"not on your nelly"},{"sense":"strong way to say no","word":"not likely"},{"sense":"strong way to say no","word":"no way"},{"sense":"strong way to say no","word":"no way Jose"},{"sense":"strong way to say no","word":"as if"},{"sense":"strong way to say no","word":"no chance"}]},"idol":{"id":"567d05e8-12f6-47bb-8e23-52d5e6977bb9","word":"idol","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"representation of anything revered","tags":["masculine"],"word":"ídolo"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"cultural icon, especially popular person","tags":["masculine"],"word":"ídolo"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"cultural icon, especially popular person","tags":["masculine"],"word":"ícone"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"20 And the rest of the men which were not killed by these plagues, yet repented not of the works of their hands, that they should not worship deuils, and idoles of golde, and siluer, and brasse, and stone, and of wood, which neither can see, nor heare, nor walke:\n21 Neither repented they of their murders, nor of their sorceries, nor of their fornication, nor of their thefts.","ref":"1611, The Holy Bible, […] (King James Version), London: […] Robert Barker, […], →OCLC, Revelation 9:20–21:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[154,160]],"id":"20809f94-415e-4111-a59f-63e418787e9e"},{"text":"Sunning himself on the board steps, I saw for the first time Mr. Farquhar Fenelon Cooke. He was dressed out in broad gaiters and bright tweeds, like an English tourist, and his face might have belonged to Dagon, idol of the Philistines.","ref":"1897 December (indicated as 1898), Winston Churchill, chapter II, in The Celebrity: An Episode, New York, N.Y.: The Macmillan Company; London: Macmillan & Co., Ltd., →OCLC:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[212,216]],"id":"f38efc7a-a879-4c1d-9603-5f7629f027a3"},{"text":"There's a one-eyed yellow idol to the north of Kathmandu, There's a little marble cross below the town; There's a broken-hearted woman tends the grave of Mad Carew, And the Yellow God forever gazes down.","ref":"1911, J. Milton Hayes, The Green Eye of the Little Yellow God:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[26,30]],"id":"0273eafd-41fd-41d5-af0b-7e429f021404"}],"links":[["image","image"],["representation","representation"],["revered","revered"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations","Quotation templates to be cleaned"],"glosses":["A graven image or representation of anything that is revered, or believed to convey spiritual power."],"id":"fea33d81-02bd-4f33-bd6f-d929e41fc690"},{"links":[["icon","icon"],["person","person"]],"glosses":["A cultural icon, or especially popular person."],"id":"d06c6827-b649-4e5e-99a2-848212611c62"},{"examples":[{"text":"Tom Cruise is his idol.","bold_text_offsets":[[18,22]],"type":"example","id":"8aa9a9ef-1858-4131-a1c5-6179f751cb30"},{"text":"Sachin Tendulkar is Rohan's idol.","bold_text_offsets":[[28,32]],"type":"example","id":"ff4e1cac-85dc-4da7-8e42-23dad52a92ef"},{"text":"They are known as \"idols\" and their job is \"to sell dreams\". For decades, the young pop stars of Japan and South Korea have been the envy of teenagers.","ref":"[2016 January 26, Mariko Oi, “The dark side of Asia’s pop music industry”, in BBC News:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[19,24]],"id":"0534dfbc-06c9-4c79-b18e-afbb2e5c9c0e"}],"categories":["Asian English","English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples","Japanese English"],"raw_glosses":["(Asia, originally Japan) A popular entertainer, usually young, captivating and attractive, and often female, with an image of being close to fans."],"qualifier":"Asia","glosses":["A popular entertainer, usually young, captivating and attractive, and often female, with an image of being close to fans."],"id":"aa610203-829f-423b-ba71-d5d364406efd"},{"categories":["English terms with obsolete senses"],"links":[["eidolon","eidolon"],["phantom","phantom"]],"raw_glosses":["(obsolete) An eidolon or phantom; a misleading or elusive image or representation."],"glosses":["An eidolon or phantom; a misleading or elusive image or representation."],"tags":["obsolete"],"id":"3a3f051a-f5b8-4ee8-be6e-e2390d6dd96f"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[{"sense":"honored statue of a deity","word":"pagod"},{"tags":["archaic"],"sense":"honored statue of a deity","english":"chiefly S & SE Asia","translation":"chiefly S & SE Asia","word":"pagoda"},{"sense":"a celebrated person","word":"icon"},{"sense":"a celebrated person","word":"star"},{"sense":"a celebrated person","word":"superstar"}]},"Ido":{"id":"d74c3d69-4133-4c6b-a047-1f3655160662","word":"Ido","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"artificial language reformed from Esperanto","tags":["masculine"],"word":"ido"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"links":[["constructed language","constructed language"],["reform","reform"],["Esperanto","Esperanto"],["Idiom Neutral","Idiom Neutral"]],"glosses":["A constructed language; a reform of Esperanto and Idiom Neutral."],"categories":["English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English proper nouns","English terms borrowed from Ido","English terms derived from Esperanto","English terms derived from Ido","English uncountable nouns","Entries with translation boxes","Mandarin terms with redundant transliterations","Pages with 5 entries","Pages with entries","Rhymes:English/aɪdəʊ","Rhymes:English/aɪdəʊ/2 syllables","Rhymes:English/iːdəʊ","Rhymes:English/iːdəʊ/2 syllables","Terms with Arabic translations","Terms with Armenian t